Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:43:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] gfxstream: optionally reuse destroyed buffer views

debug.velox.bufferview_cache=1: a buffer view the application destroys stays
alive on the host and is returned again for an identical create (same device,
buffer, format, offset and range; no flags or pNext). At most 1024 views are
kept. Cached views of a buffer are destroyed before the buffer and those of a
device before the device, since the host may reuse handle values. Saves a
synchronous create and an asynchronous destroy per reuse. vkCreateBufferView
and vkDestroyBufferView now go through the resource tracker (functable.py and
the regenerated func_table.cpp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
